{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Adam Matthew Vinatieri (born December 28, 1972) is an American football placekicker for the Indianapolis Colts of the National Football League (NFL).","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has played in five Super Bowls: four with the New England Patriots and one with the Colts.","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Vinatieri won Super Bowls in 2001, 2003, and 2004 with the Patriots, as well as in 2006 with the Colts.","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Among placekickers, he holds NFL records for most Super Bowl appearances (5) and most Super Bowl wins (4).","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He also holds NFL records, among all players, for most postseason points scored (234), and most overtime field goals made (10).","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He is the only player ever to score 1,000 points with two different teams.","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" As of the 2016 season, Vinatieri, 44, is the oldest active player in the NFL.","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Vinatieri has converted the 3rd most field-goals in NFL history (529) as well as attempted the 4th most field-goals in NFL history (627), 12 behind George Blanda.","title":"Adam Vinatieri"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"James Nathaniel Brown (born February 17, 1936) is a former professional American football player and actor.","title":"Jim Brown"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was a fullback for the Cleveland Browns of the National Football League (NFL) from 1957 through 1965.","title":"Jim Brown"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Considered to be among the greatest football players of all time, Brown was a Pro Bowl invitee every season he was in the league, was recognized as the AP NFL Most Valuable Player three times, and won an NFL championship with the Browns in 1964.","title":"Jim Brown"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He led the league in rushing yards in